"""
Connectors of `SimpleDieselEngine`, without any equation. Parameter-preset wrappers
extend this, hold one `SimpleDieselEngine` as `core` and connect each port to it, so
a preset can replace `SimpleDieselEngine` in an assembly without rewiring.

The meaning, units and sampling rules of every port are those documented on
`SimpleDieselEngine`.
"""
partial component DieselEnginePorts
  RPM_demand = RealInput()
  "Net shaft work [kWh], signed"
  KWh = RealOutput()
  "Cumulative fuel mass [kg], nondecreasing"
  Fuel = RealOutput()
  "Cumulative fuel mass [kg] metered with a held SFOC end value"
  Fuel_extrapolated = RealOutput()
  "Fuel mass rate [kg/s], never negative"
  Inst_Fuel = RealOutput()
  "Signed shaft power [W], positive when the engine drives the shaft"
  ShaftPower = RealOutput()
  "SFOC table coverage: 1 while the brake power is inside the table range (or zero), 0 while a held end value is in use"
  SFOC_valid = RealOutput()
  flange = Spline()
end
